import AxQM.Postulates.API.Evolution
import ToMathlib.Analysis.CStarAlgebra.Unitary.ExpEndomorphism

/-!
# The Hamiltonian generator of a unitary evolution, with bounded spectrum

Nielsen & Chuang, *Quantum Computation and Quantum Information*, Problem 4.3(1) asks to show that,
for a unitary `U` on `n` qubits, `H ≡ i ln(U)` is **Hermitian, with eigenvalues in the range `0` to
`2π`**. In this library a closed-system dynamics is an `Evolution` (a bundled unitary) and a
Hamiltonian is an `Observable` (a bundled self-adjoint operator); `Observable.propagator H 1 0 1` is
the unit-time, `ℏ = 1` propagator `exp(-i H)` (Nielsen–Chuang eq. 2.91).

The existence half — *every* `Evolution` has a Hermitian generator — is
`AxQM.Evolution.exists_hamiltonian_generator` (`AxQM/NC/Ch4/Problem4_3.lean`). This file adds
the **eigenvalue-range refinement**: the generator can be chosen with its spectrum contained in
`[0, 2π]`.

* `AxQM.Evolution.exists_hamiltonian_generator_spectrum_Icc` — for any `Evolution U`, there
  is an `Observable H` with `U = H.propagator 1 0 1` (i.e. `U = exp(-iH)`) **and** every eigenvalue
  of `H` a real number in `[0, 2π]` (`spectrum ℂ H.op ⊆ ℝ ∩ [0, 2π]`). This is exactly Problem
  4.3(1): with the appropriate branch of `ln`, `H = i ln U` is Hermitian with spectrum in `[0, 2π]`.

## Design

* **The mathematics.** The operator-level fact — every unitary on a finite-dimensional complex
  Hilbert space is `exp(-i • A)` for a self-adjoint `A` with `spectrum ℂ A ⊆ ℝ ∩ [0, 2π]` — is the
  general lemma
  `ContinuousLinearMap.exists_isSelfAdjoint_spectrum_Icc_exp_neg_smul_I_eq_of_mem_unitary`,
  proved by a `[0, 2π)`-branch of the logarithm via the continuous functional calculus. Here
  `H.op = A`, so
  `H.propagator 1 0 1 = exp(-i H) = exp(-i • A) = U`.
* **Spectrum over `ℂ`.** The bound reads `spectrum ℂ H.op ⊆ Complex.ofReal '' [0, 2π]` — every
  eigenvalue is a *real* number in `[0, 2π]` — which is the faithful content of "eigenvalues in the
  range `0` to `2π`" for the Hermitian `H`, and avoids the `Algebra ℝ`/`IsScalarTower` scaffolding a
  `spectrum ℝ` phrasing would require. See that lemma's docstring.
* **Generality.** N&C fix a unitary on `n` qubits (dimension `2ⁿ`); the theorem is stated for an
  arbitrary finite-dimensional system `S`, which is strictly more general and specialises to the
  `n`-qubit register. Part (1) makes no use of the tensor factorisation.
-/

open scoped InnerProductSpace

noncomputable section

namespace AxQM

variable {S : QSystem}

/-- **Nielsen & Chuang, Problem 4.3(1): the Hamiltonian generator can be chosen with spectrum in
`[0, 2π]`.** Every closed-system `Evolution U` on a finite-dimensional quantum system `S` is
generated by a Hamiltonian `H` (an `Observable`, i.e. a self-adjoint operator) with
`U = H.propagator 1 0 1` — that is, `U = exp(-iH)` — whose eigenvalues are all real numbers in
`[0, 2π]` (`spectrum ℂ H.op ⊆ Complex.ofReal '' Set.Icc 0 (2π)`).

This is the full content of "`H = i ln(U)` is Hermitian, with eigenvalues in the range `0` to `2π`":
choosing the `[0, 2π)`-branch of `ln`, the generator's spectrum lands in `[0, 2π]`. It refines the
existence statement `Evolution.exists_hamiltonian_generator` (`AxQM/NC/Ch4/Problem4_3.lean`) with
the eigenvalue-range clause. -/
theorem Evolution.exists_hamiltonian_generator_spectrum_Icc (U : Evolution S) :
    ∃ H : Observable S, U = H.propagator 1 0 1 ∧
      spectrum ℂ H.op ⊆ Complex.ofReal '' Set.Icc 0 (2 * Real.pi) := by
  have : CompleteSpace S.space := FiniteDimensional.completeSpace ℂ S.space
  -- The unitary `U.op = exp(-i • A)` for a self-adjoint `A` with spectrum in `[0, 2π]`.
  obtain ⟨A, hAsa, hAspec, hAexp⟩ :=
    ContinuousLinearMap.exists_isSelfAdjoint_spectrum_Icc_exp_neg_smul_I_eq_of_mem_unitary U.unitary
  -- Take the Hamiltonian `H` with `H.op = A`; then `exp(-i H) = exp(-i • A) = U.op`.
  refine ⟨⟨A, hAsa⟩, Evolution.ext ?_, hAspec⟩
  rw [Observable.propagator_op, ← hAexp]
  norm_num

end AxQM
